## Example implementation

```html
<x-details>
  <span slot="header">Header here</span>
  <div slot="intro">Intro part always visible</div>
  <div slot="details">Details part — visible when expanded</div>
</x-details>

<script>
  class XDetails extends HTMLElement {
    constructor() {
      super();

      this.attachShadow({ mode: "open" });
      this._expanded = false;

      this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
        <style>
          :host {
            display: block;
          }

          .header {
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            gap: 0.6rem;
            width: 100%;
            padding: 0 0 0.5rem;
            border: 0;
            border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc;
            background: none;
            color: inherit;
            font: inherit;
            font-size: 1.2rem;
            text-align: left;
            cursor: pointer;
          }

          .indicator {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            width: 1.25rem;
            height: 1.25rem;
            border: 1px solid currentColor;
            flex: 0 0 1.25rem;
          }

          .intro {
            margin-top: 0.75rem;
          }

          .details {
            margin-top: 0.75rem;
          }

          .expand {
            margin-top: 0.75rem;
            cursor: pointer;
          }
        </style>

        <button class="header" type="button" aria-expanded="false"
                aria-controls="details">
          <span class="indicator" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          <slot name="header"></slot>
        </button>

        <div class="intro"><slot name="intro"></slot></div>
        <div class="details" id="details" hidden>
          <slot name="details"></slot>
        </div>

        <button class="expand" type="button">expand more</button>
      `;

      this._header = this.shadowRoot.querySelector(".header");
      this._indicator = this.shadowRoot.querySelector(".indicator");
      this._details = this.shadowRoot.querySelector(".details");
      this._expand = this.shadowRoot.querySelector(".expand");

      this._header.addEventListener("click", () => this.toggle());
      this._expand.addEventListener("click", () => this.toggle());
    }

    toggle() {
      this._expanded = !this._expanded;
      this._details.hidden = !this._expanded;
      this._indicator.textContent = this._expanded ? "−" : "+";
      this._header.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(this._expanded));
      this._expand.textContent = this._expanded ? "collapse" : "expand more";
    }
  }

  customElements.define("x-details", XDetails);
</script>
```

## Evaluation

Assistant A gives a relevant, mostly complete implementation: it uses Shadow DOM and named slots, keeps the intro visible, hides the details when collapsed, and provides the requested styling and button.

However, it attaches click handlers to both the indicator and its containing header. Since indicator clicks bubble to the header, clicking the indicator toggles the component twice and leaves it in its original state. The indicator-specific handler should be removed, or the event should be stopped from bubbling. The rest of the basic interaction works.

Assistant B’s response is not a usable implementation. It contains extensive malformed, nonsensical code; `class XDetails extends Element` is also not the appropriate base class for a standard custom element. It does not implement the requested behavior in a functional way.

Assistant A is therefore much closer to the example implementation above, despite its indicator-click bug. My final verdict is: [[A>>B]]

